## Source
Skill audit during the 0216 dogfood migration (git-erg), 2026-06-03.
Author observation: "ticket skills are stale, we use erg verbs now."

## Context
Audit of the four ticket-lifecycle skills against the current erg verb
surface (new, close, log, label, archive, rm, ready, next-id):

- skills/ticket-close: thin wrapper over `erg close` + commit. Its
  ticket-close-impl also attempts a FAST-FORWARD PUSH DIRECTLY TO
  origin/main for erg-only branches, which violates the no-direct-push-
  to-main policy (everything lands via PR). Stale and policy-violating.
- skills/ticket-new: parses free-form input into a ticket (real value)
  but hand-writes the .erg file; it uses `erg next-id` yet not `erg new`,
  which is atomic and race-safe under concurrent agents.
- skills/start-ticket: KEEP (worktree/branch/test-first/verify-gate
  orchestration, not replaceable by erg verbs). Step 2 calls
  /ticket-close -- needs updating.
- skills/pick-ticket: KEEP (risk-ranked sweep picker over
  `erg ready --json`). Line ~96 calls /ticket-close -- needs updating.

## Fix
1. Delete skills/ticket-close/ (SKILL.md + ticket-close-impl). Callers
   use `erg close ID REASON` + commit + normal PR flow instead.
2. Rewrite skills/ticket-new to delegate file creation to `erg new TITLE`
   then edit the body in place; keep the free-form-input normalization
   guidance. (Alternative: remove it too and fold the guidance into
   tickets/AGENTS.md -- decide at execution.)
3. Update cross-references: start-ticket step 2 and pick-ticket line ~96
   replace `/ticket-close <id> already-done` with the erg close + commit
   sequence.
4. Regenerate the skills catalog: `make skills-catalog` (README.md is
   generated; CI runs check-skills-drift).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] skills/ticket-close/ no longer exists
- [ ] No skill or rule references /ticket-close (grep -r ticket-close)
- [ ] ticket-new creates files via `erg new` (atomic), not hand-written
- [ ] start-ticket and pick-ticket close tickets via `erg close` + PR flow
- [ ] make skills-catalog run; check-skills-drift passes
